landed: done (2026-07-10)
--------------------------

T1 (bridge): load a fixture, unload it, load it fresh again -- all
three ok. T2 (scala unit, Fake_Backend): both error paths, never-
loaded and image-tier, are clean isErrors naming the reason.

Implementation note (a genuine engine-level finding, not just a
detail): the plan's step 1 said "session.unload_theories + purge_
theories (shared with check_theory's purge step)" -- that shared purge
step turned out to be actively harmful (see plans/check_theory's
status block for the full story: Headless.Resources.purge_theories
never pushes its edits to the live document, so calling it directly
desyncs Resources' bookkeeping from the prover and the next reload
corrupts the document). check_theory dropped the purge entirely, but
unload_theory genuinely needs a document-level removal, not just a
fresh read -- so it goes through Resources.clean_theories instead
(unload_theories + purge_theories(None) + session.update in one
state.change), the one purge path that keeps its own bookkeeping
consistent with the live document. Its blast radius is session-wide
(purge_theories(None) sweeps every currently-unrequired node, not just
the target theory) -- harmless here since MCP_Session never keeps a
theory "required" past the end of its own use_theories call, but worth
knowing if that assumption ever changes.

Also: unload_theory's inputSchema is just {name} (per the plan, no
master_dir), but resolving name -> Document.Node.Name needs the same
master_dir the theory was loaded with. MCP_Session now records name ->
master_dir on every successful load_theory/check_theory, so unload_
theory can resolve without asking for it again; the same map doubles
as the "was this ever loaded" registry for T2's not-loaded error path.

T3 (repls surviving/breaking an unload) stays deferred: it needs
repl_init_from_source ("attach"), a still-deferred wave-1 tool, to
create a repl from the theory's document in the first place. T4 (scope
drop) stays deferred to plans/scope_add, as planned. T5 (full chain):
covered as part of the e2e wave-2 block in mcp/test/test_mcp.py (load
-> check_theory staleness -> unload -> unload-again-is-error).

Four-layer test locations: scala unit in mcp_test/src/
mcp_handler_tests.scala; bridge in mcp_test/src/mcp_bridge_tests.scala
("wave 2: unload_theory T1 ..."); e2e in mcp/test/test_mcp.py
("wave 2: tools/call unload_theory ..."). No ml-unit layer.
